{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["C13", "C14", "FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.20", "FCC1.VCAP1", "FCC1.VCAP2"],
      "nets": ["VREF+_FCC", "FCC1.VCAP1", "FCC1.VCAP2"],
      "observed": "On the Flight Control Computer sheet the 2.2 uF capacitors C13 and C14 (carrying the note 'C13, C14: ESR < 100mOhm') are tied to the VREF+_FCC net at FCC1 pin 20 (VREF+), the same net that already has its proper reference filter (R21 47, C29 1u, C30 100n) on the right of the sheet. The STM32H753's VCAP1/VCAP2 pins are left with no decoupling capacitors. By contrast, on the Navigation Computer sheet the identical 2.2 uF low‑ESR caps C37/C38 (note 'C37, C38: ESR < 100mOhm') are correctly placed on the VCAP_1/VCAP_2 pins of NAVC1.",
      "expected": "The 2.2 uF low‑ESR capacitors belong on the H753's VCAP1/VCAP2 pins (the internal‑regulator output, which requires a low‑ESR bulk cap for stability); VREF+ only needs the small 100 nF/1 uF filter that is already present. The 'ESR < 100mOhm' requirement quoted on the FCC sheet is a VCAP‑pin requirement, not a VREF+ requirement.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC sheet: 'C13, C14: ESR < 100mOhm' with C13 2u2 / C14 2u2 connected to the VREF+ pin (20) / VREF+_FCC net; VREF+_FCC also filtered by R21 47, C29 1u, C30 100n"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NAVC sheet: 'C37, C38: ESR < 100mOhm' with C37 2u2 / C38 2u2 connected to VCAP_1 / VCAP_2 of STM32F405RGTx"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Flight Control Computer MCU | FCC1 | STM32H753VITx (Cortex‑M7, 400 MHz, 2 MB flash, LQFP‑100)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The H753 internal regulator outputs (VCAP1/VCAP2) are undecoupled, so the core supply is unstable; the MCU is likely to brown‑out, fail to boot, or reset randomly. VREF+ is additionally over‑loaded with 2.2 uF, degrading reference settling/noise.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power section, I2C/GPIO/UART inter‑MCU links, sensors, PWM driver, flash/EEPROM and the documented barometer pin‑swap all match the specification, but on the FCC sheet the 2.2 uF low‑ESR decoupling capacitors (C13/C14) are wired to VREF+ instead of the STM32H753's VCAP1/VCAP2 pins (which are left undecoupled), unlike the correctly wired C37/C38 on the NAVC sheet — a misplacement that would leave the H753's internal regulator unstable."
}

